# UI Components Development Rules

## Component Architecture

- Use Lit Element for lightweight Web Components
- Implement reactive properties with @property decorator
- Use @state for internal component state
- Follow single responsibility principle
- Create composable and reusable components

## Styling Guidelines

- Use CSS Custom Properties for theming
- Integrate with VSCode theme variables
- Implement responsive design patterns
- Use CSS Grid and Flexbox for layouts
- Follow consistent spacing and typography

## Component Communication

- Use Custom Events for component interaction
- Implement proper event bubbling and capturing
- Use structured data for event payloads
- Handle event cleanup in component lifecycle
- Implement proper error handling for events

## Accessibility

- Use semantic HTML elements
- Implement proper ARIA attributes
- Ensure keyboard navigation support
- Provide screen reader compatibility
- Use appropriate color contrast ratios

## Performance

- Minimize DOM updates with Lit's rendering
- Use efficient property change detection
- Implement lazy loading for heavy components
- Cache expensive computations
- Use proper disposal patterns

## Testing

- Write unit tests for component logic
- Test user interactions and events
- Validate accessibility compliance
- Test theme integration
- Ensure cross-browser compatibility

## Documentation

- Document component props and events
- Provide usage examples
- Document styling customization options
- Include accessibility notes
- Maintain changelog for breaking changes

